From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:19:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 33/49] fix(gastown): make patrol wisp reconcile see the wisp
 it is running (gcp-ah8h)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

gcp-xbl landed FACET 1 of the reconcile bug (`--include-infra`) at every site
and left FACET 2 (`--status=in_progress`) unfixed at every site. Facet 2 alone
is sufficient to break reconcile, so the bug gcp-xbl described stayed live at
the pin the whole city runs.

`GC_BEAD_ID` is unset in coordination-agent sessions, so the fallback query is
what actually runs. Patrol wisps are poured `open` and nothing transitions them
to `in_progress`, so `--status=in_progress` matched nothing and CURRENT_WISP
resolved empty on a normal cycle. With CURRENT_WISP empty the surplus exclusion
`select(.id != $cur)` excluded nothing, the wisp being executed landed in its
own surplus set, no successor was poured, and the patrol loop stopped advancing
— every command exiting 0, the only signal a log line that read like a benign
guard.

All seven fallback sites now query `--status=open,in_progress --limit=0`, the
same filter their sibling surplus query already used. Matching filters also
guarantee CURRENT_WISP is the element that query lists first, so the exclusion
always lands.

Resolving CURRENT_WISP empty is now a fail-closed error at the point of
resolution, before the surplus set is computed or a successor is poured, rather
than a quiet echo discovered afterwards. The witness burn step was the one site
that echoed and continued with no exit at all; it now drains and exits 1 like
its deacon counterpart. Every remaining "could not resolve" message names the
consequence instead of reading as routine.

Sites fixed:
  mol-deacon-patrol.toml:713
  mol-witness-patrol.toml:744
  mol-refinery-patrol.toml:151, 299, 400, 718, 1707

gcp-xbl relied on a manual re-grep to confirm it had landed, which is how it
shipped closed and half-applied. tests/test_wisp_molecule_queries.py — the
guard that already pins facet 1 — now pins facet 2 too: a `--type=molecule`
query filtering `in_progress` must also cover `open`, and a live-wisp query
must use `--limit=0` so it cannot desynchronise from the unlimited surplus
query. The witness startup protocol's deliberate two-query union is recognised
by adjacency, so it needs no opt-out marker.

Verified red against the pre-fix pin e9c2218 (exactly 7 violations, matching
the site list above) and green on this tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
